WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
Why should you watch One Piece? Where do I&nbsp;
even start! Maybe you just keep stumbling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:14.700
across this anime and finally have given in to&nbsp;
find out what all the hype is about. With only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.780
a few years to go left in the series,&nbsp;
and the beginnign of the final saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:25.020
now’s the perfect time to come aboard the Straw&nbsp;
Hat’s ship and sail to the One Piece along with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:30.180
the rest of the fandom. Or you might already&nbsp;
be a full-on believer and know how absolutely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:35.580
earth-shatteringly brilliant this piece of&nbsp;
fiction is and we just can’t help but want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.980
everyone you know to experience it, too. Like&nbsp;
me for my mate Daidus, who asked me for a video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.980 --> 00:01:51.360
on why he should start One Piece. Here is the&nbsp;
super short, really not long at all answer.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.840
Chapter 1: A brief history of One PIece

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.800
I don’t know if you’ve ever tried to convince&nbsp;
someone to take the plunge and read the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.800
but it can be a hard sell. Watching a 26&nbsp;
episode series can be enough of a commitment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:15.780
but asking someone to read 1,000 chapters? It&nbsp;
can seem downright daunting. Not to mention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:22.080
maybe some people are turned off by the cartoonish&nbsp;
art style, thinking it’s not as serious or cool as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.940
some of their other favorite series. Well,&nbsp;
I’m here to change your mind abou that.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:34.320
Thanks to a…questionable… 4Kids dub, and a&nbsp;
few other factors, One Piece has had a hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:40.080
time growing its fanbase in the West compared to&nbsp;
series like Dragon Ball or Naruto, but let’s look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:50.940
at the facts: This is the most successful manga&nbsp;
of all time. One Piece has outsold every other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:56.580
comic series but Superman. Its sales numbers&nbsp;
have beaten out both Spiderman and Batman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:04.740
whose publication histories predate One Piece&nbsp;
by decades. Estimated sales placed Eiichiro Oda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:12.180
within the top 10 best selling authors of all&nbsp;
time. He’s just passed Dr. Seuss and soon One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:20.760
Piece will even outsell Harry Potter. Simply put,&nbsp;
One Piece, with a serialization spanning 25 years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:26.820
is a worldwide sales juggernaut.&nbsp;
Why? Because it’s just that good.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.780
Before we get started, though, you might&nbsp;
want to know some of the basics - so what’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:37.500
One Piece about? One Piece takes place 20 years&nbsp;
after the execution of the King of the Pirates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:43.320
Gol D. Roger. On the executioner’s stand, Roger&nbsp;
announced to the world that he left his treasure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:48.600
the One Piece, hidden somewhere out in the&nbsp;
world’s most dangerous sea, the Grand Line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:54.600
a terrifying strip of ocean that spans&nbsp;
the globe. The announcement of this great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.600 --> 00:04:01.500
treasure lead to a great age of piracy, which&nbsp;
brings us to our protagonist, Monkey D. Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:07.620
a rambunctious young pirate who has rubber powers&nbsp;
thanks to eating a devil fruit - a magical fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:15.060
that bestows special abilities to someone who&nbsp;
eats them, but renders them unable to swim (a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:21.180
pretty big drawback in a story that takes place&nbsp;
on the high seas). Throughout Luffy’s adventure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:28.260
he gathers together a crew who fight by&nbsp;
his side as he takes on rival pirates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:33.240
and the world government in an attempt&nbsp;
to find the world’s greatest treasure.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:39.120
There are four qualities that make One Piece&nbsp;
stand out among its peers: The world building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.700
the plot, the characters, and the tone. Are&nbsp;
there more qualities than just these that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:51.060
make One Piece fantastic? Of course, but we don’t&nbsp;
want to go into any dangerous spoiler territory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:56.640
and dampen your experience of the series. So&nbsp;
without further ado, let’s get into chapter 2:

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.380
Teh World Of One PIece

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:04.140
If you ask the average fan what their favorite&nbsp;
thing about One Piece is, a lot of them will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:09.120
say its outstanding world building. If&nbsp;
all you’ve seen is promotional images,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:14.940
it probably seems like One Piece is just a nice&nbsp;
little story where our crew sails around getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:21.060
into hijinx. What I definitely wasn’t ready for&nbsp;
when I started the series was a complex web of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:26.820
political intrigue that easily stands on the level&nbsp;
of a series like Game of Thrones or Lord of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:33.180
Rings. If you enjoy fleshed out fantasy worlds,&nbsp;
you’ll fall in love with the world of One Piece.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:38.580
This world is filled with pirates searching for&nbsp;
the ultimate treasure, the One Piece, but along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:45.600
the way our crew visits several islands, each with&nbsp;
its own unique government, culture, creatures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:51.480
etc. One island may be filled with prehistoric&nbsp;
dinosaurs and battling giants, whereas the next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:57.120
is an expansive desert kingdom. One island may&nbsp;
be based on feudal Japan and the other might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:02.880
a dream-fueled candyland straight out of a Disney&nbsp;
movie. And the wild thing is that all of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:09.300
diverse places form a cohesive whole. We don’t&nbsp;
simply stop off and then sail away into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:15.780
horizon, never to think about those past islands&nbsp;
again. Instead, they all interact seamlessly with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:22.260
one another. Each kingdom or island the Straw&nbsp;
Hats visit are connected politically through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:27.900
the World Government, a shadowy organization&nbsp;
that claims to uphold the peace and defend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:35.400
people from evil pirates, but in reality causes&nbsp;
just as much suffering as those pirates do.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:40.740
The world of One Piece is composed of many&nbsp;
factions that move independently from our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:46.140
main characters. And while Straw Hat Luffy&nbsp;
certainly makes his mark on the world, he’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:53.040
just one small fish in a very big pond. While the&nbsp;
story sagas are shaped by the Straw Hats’ actions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:58.740
the world is always moving and shifting behind&nbsp;
the scenes as well. Between each major story arc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:04.380
Oda shows us what the major players of the world&nbsp;
are up to elsewhere. In no other series will you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:11.340
see a fanbase get so ecstatic about something as&nbsp;
seemingly simple as a newspaper, but when Big News&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:17.220
Morgans drops the latest issue you better believe&nbsp;
we’re about to get some mind-blowing updates.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:25.920
Simply put, this world doesn’t seem like a game&nbsp;
board for pieces to move around on. It feels like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:33.600
a real living, breathing place and we care deeply&nbsp;
about its many inhabitants. Oda has filled each of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:39.180
these islands with so much care and consideration&nbsp;
that we’re on the edge of our seats while we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:46.020
wait to see how the complex political dynamics&nbsp;
play out. And that is all thanks to chapter 3:

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:46.800
The Characters

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:53.580
And we have to talk about the stars of&nbsp;
the show, the incredible characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.580 --> 00:08:00.480
and wow does One Piece have some fantastic ones.&nbsp;
I mean, with over 1,000 characters in the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:07.440
there’s a little something for everyone here,&nbsp;
but central to One Piece is the Straw Hat Crew.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:13.080
Our main character, Monkey D. Luffy, is unlike&nbsp;
any other shonen protagonist. On the surface,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:19.260
he seems to share some traits with other heroes.&nbsp;
He’s got the brains - or lack thereof - of Goku,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:25.860
and a lofty goal like Naruto, but no one has the&nbsp;
conviction that Luffy does. And while he wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:31.440
do too well on his standardized tests, he has an&nbsp;
intuitive emotional intelligence that allows him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:37.080
to make friends everywhere he goes. More than&nbsp;
his rubber body, his true power is the way that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:42.840
he relates to others and fights for those he&nbsp;
cares about. Most of the time he’s carefree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:49.200
silly even, but when it’s time to get serious,&nbsp;
he’ll send a chill up your spine and you’ll be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:54.420
cheering for him when he gives villains what&nbsp;
they deserve (usually a really big punch).

00:08:54.420 --> 00:09:00.840
The rest of the crew is also fantastic.&nbsp;
The absolute badass swordsman, Zoro;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:06.420
the greedy navigator, Nami; the cowardly&nbsp;
sniper, Usopp; the suave chef, Sanji;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:12.360
the cotton-candy loving reindeer doctor, Chopper,&nbsp;
and a singing skeleton named Brook. As well as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:17.100
some others that I won’t spoil for now because&nbsp;
their joining can come as a bit of a surprise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:22.500
Every one of these characters not only has&nbsp;
spectacular feats, but they have dreams and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:28.200
convictions that match their captain’s dream to&nbsp;
become the pirate king. And while they’re fun and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:34.320
even silly on the surface, they all have depth.&nbsp;
As we learn about the tragedies they suffered in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:40.200
childhood that made them who they are today, we&nbsp;
fall in love with this cast of characters. Also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:46.680
you will definitely 100% cry when you get to&nbsp;
their backstories…so just be ready for that.

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:52.620
Of course, our main crew are only the beginning.&nbsp;
The Straw Hats also encounter many others on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:58.140
their travels and some standouts are the&nbsp;
amazing villains. The Marines are tasked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:02.580
by the World Government to hunt down the&nbsp;
lawbreaking pirates, which means our main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:08.760
cast are on the run from fearsome members like&nbsp;
Captain Smoker or Admiral Akainu. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:12.900
there are also oopposing pirates such&nbsp;
as the Seven Warlords of the Sea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:18.720
which includes fierce and intimidating characters&nbsp;
like the criminal mastermind, Sir Crocodile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:24.360
or the greatest swordsman in the world, Hawkeyes&nbsp;
Mihawk. When we’re introduced to these characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:30.240
they are insurmountable obstacles - some&nbsp;
of them are literally impossible to even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:37.320
touch. It makes it all the more satisfying when&nbsp;
Luffy and his crew use their resolve to overcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:41.460
these villains and save the innocent&nbsp;
people on the islands they encounter.

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:46.980
And speaking of those innocent people, the Straw&nbsp;
Hats have their fair share of allies on the seas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:51.000
of the Grand Line, too. Some are royalty&nbsp;
who rule the various islands they visit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:57.060
such as Nefertari Vivi, the princess of&nbsp;
Alabasta, but some are even fellow pirates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:01.920
like the fan favorite Trafalgar Law.
And then there are the legends who either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:07.320
in the past or present have shaped the One&nbsp;
Piece world itself: People like Gol D. Roger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:12.720
the pirate who on the execution stand, started&nbsp;
the great age of piracy by telling people across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:17.640
the world to search for his treasure, the One&nbsp;
Piece. Throughout the adventure of One Piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:23.400
you’ll meet a fascinating cast of characters. And&nbsp;
if it sounds like a lot, well, no worries there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:30.840
Oda takes his time in each location to&nbsp;
let us get to know these characters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:35.940
to fully develop them. It’s one of&nbsp;
the reasons that One Piece’s length&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:41.940
works in its favor - it’s all killer,&nbsp;
no filler. Which brings me to chapter 4:

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:42.720
The Plot

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:48.960
The plot of One Piece is another fantastic&nbsp;
reason you should read this series. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:53.400
amazing thing about One Piece isn’t that&nbsp;
it has over 1,000 chapters. It’s that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:58.440
has 1,000 chapters and it’s still going&nbsp;
strong - the arcs being published right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:04.860
now are some of the best One Piece has to offer.
There’s a simple reason for this - The mangaka,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:09.540
Eiichiro Oda, planned his story from&nbsp;
the beginning. I know that seems simple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:14.820
but you’d be amazed how many authors don’t&nbsp;
know how their story will end when they begin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:19.320
publication - they just kind of start from&nbsp;
a premise and make it up as they go along.

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:25.080
25 years ago, Luffy set out to find the ultimate&nbsp;
treasure - the One Piece. He’s still searching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:30.360
for that treasure. And many are skeptical that&nbsp;
whatever’s revealed will be disappointing - like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:36.420
the treasure will be “the friends they made along&nbsp;
the way.” However, Oda has gone on record saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:42.840
that the treasure is something physical. He’s&nbsp;
had the final panel and the overall story of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:48.000
the series planned for decades. And while&nbsp;
he does insert fun details and ideas along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:54.600
the way to expand on the world he’s created, the&nbsp;
broad strokes of the story are well thought out.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:58.080
It would have been one thing to have&nbsp;
a great idea for a pirate adventure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:02.520
and just letting Luffy start his journey&nbsp;
without having the end in mind. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:08.820
he may have run out of ideas. But ever since&nbsp;
the beginning, Oda has been constructing a story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:14.640
with this singular goal. Which, honestly, makes&nbsp;
it an impressive series not just among manga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:19.740
but among literature in general.
One way we see this is with Oda’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:24.540
masterful hints and foreshadowing. Characters&nbsp;
will be mentioned in the early beginnings of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:31.980
story only to show up and play a larger role&nbsp;
hundreds of chapters later. It just goes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:37.140
show the thoughtful planning that went into&nbsp;
creating this masterfully structured story.

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:42.000
Not to take digs too hard at other series, but&nbsp;
many of them seem to be developed based on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:48.480
central, interesting premise, but eventually&nbsp;
fall apart because the storytellers didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:53.880
begin with the ending in mind. We’ll call it&nbsp;
the J.J. Abrams effect. To leave the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:58.440
of anime momentarily, we can think about how&nbsp;
TV shows like LOST or the much maligned Star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:04.560
Wars Sequel Trilogy begin by Abrams setting up&nbsp;
many mysteries, so fans get sucked in by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:10.620
intrigue. The problem is that Abrams has not&nbsp;
figured out what the solution to the mystery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:17.460
is and seemingly doesn’t care, leading to his&nbsp;
properties having terribly disappointing endings.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:25.560
Many Shonen seem to suffer from similar problems.&nbsp;
For instance in Bleach, the Soul Society was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:32.640
fantastic early arc. However, it seemed like Tite&nbsp;
Kubo wasn’t sure what should happen afterward…so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:37.920
they rinsed and repeated with a new kidnapped&nbsp;
ally to rescue and a new assortment of powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:43.440
baddies to fight. Dragon Ball Z kind of does&nbsp;
this, too. And who can forget the ending of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:51.300
Naruto when we found out *Big Spoiler Warning,&nbsp;
by the way…* it was aliens all along? Granted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:56.040
One Piece also has some moon and space&nbsp;
stuff going on, but that’s been well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.040 --> 00:15:01.740
established for hundreds of chapters instead&nbsp;
of suddenly appearing at the very last minute!&nbsp;

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:07.920
Most shonen also deal with “power creep” -&nbsp;
the problem of running into an impossibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:11.760
strong villain, having the heroes&nbsp;
develop a new powerup to defeat them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:17.460
and then rinsing and repeating over and&nbsp;
over, until the powers are just absurd and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:21.780
don’t fit within the established scope of the&nbsp;
narrative. And while One Piece does have cool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:27.960
powers and power-ups, it avoids the problem of&nbsp;
power creep that we see in many other series.

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:33.060
In an early scene, we’re introduced to&nbsp;
one of the literal strongest characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:37.740
in the entire series - Hawkeyes Mihawk,&nbsp;
the greatest swordsman in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:41.760
one of those Seven Warlords of the Sea&nbsp;
I mentioned earlier. In that encounter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:48.060
Luffy’s crewmate Zoro, whose goal is to become&nbsp;
the world’s greatest swordsman faces off against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:53.160
him. Zoro, who we’ve seen effortlessly take out&nbsp;
opponents left and right before this moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:59.280
is absolutely annihilated by Mihawk. Thanks&nbsp;
to this scene, and some others like it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:04.500
we early on get to see the power ceiling&nbsp;
of the world. This way, future power-ups&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:10.680
don’t seem pulled out of nowhere - instead they&nbsp;
seem in line with the properties of the world.

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:20.400
The consistency of One Piece is outstanding.&nbsp;
Even the “bad” arcs - or the least favorites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:25.440
among the fandom - often surpass the&nbsp;
quality of most other series. Are there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:30.660
occasional flaws or inconsistencies?&nbsp;
Sure, Oda is surprisingly still human,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:35.460
after all. But the positives of this&nbsp;
series, especially given its massive length,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:40.920
outshine the negatives by far. And&nbsp;
this is mainly thanks to chapter 5:

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:42.600
The overall Tone

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.600
Another reason to watch One Piece - at least the&nbsp;
final reason we’ll talk about today - is its tone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:52.080
And this encapsulates a lot of things. When Matt&nbsp;
Owens, a producer on the upcoming Netflix live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:57.840
action One Piece series was talking about adapting&nbsp;
the series, he said One Piece does three things:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.840 --> 00:17:02.760
It makes you laugh, it makes you cry,&nbsp;
and it makes you say “holy shit.”

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:08.340
First and foremost something that really makes&nbsp;
One Piece stand out among its peers is its sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:13.800
of humor. Sure, other Shonen often have gags&nbsp;
and bits of humor sprinkled in, but One Piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:18.840
really has laughter baked into its core. I mean,&nbsp;
just look at some of these character designs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:28.980
And the scenarios they get themselves into can&nbsp;
be just as funny. Luffy, having rubber powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:34.500
is essentially just a stretchy cartoon man.&nbsp;
Sometimes to fight he blows himself up into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:39.120
massive balloon. Once, when fighting a character&nbsp;
with food-based powers, he valiantly ate his way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:43.860
to victory with the voracious appetite&nbsp;
that only a shonen protagonist can have.

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:52.140
Some people criticize One Piece for its wacky and&nbsp;
goofy art style, but the truth is this is one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:57.900
its greatest strengths. Not just because it’s&nbsp;
hilarious, but because it makes the emotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:57.900 --> 00:18:04.980
and serious moments hit that much harder.&nbsp;
You’ll just be sitting there enjoying your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:09.240
goofy pirate manga, when suddenly you are&nbsp;
openly sobbing. I don’t care if you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:15.300
a heart of stone. You will cry when you see&nbsp;
the suffering this cute reindeer has endured.

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:22.560
And when you see the ridiculous stakes that&nbsp;
these arcs get to, you’ll be stunned. When an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:30.240
entire country of people are at stake and the only&nbsp;
possibility of saving them means Luffy defeating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:36.900
a villain who has already utterly defeated him&nbsp;
multiple times, you’ll be on the edge of your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:42.420
seat - and even if you know deep down that things&nbsp;
will work on fine because there are still hundreds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:49.020
of chapters to go…it won’t stop you from jumping&nbsp;
for joy when Luffy finally beats that big bad.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:54.600
Lots and lots and lots of reasons that you need&nbsp;
to check out One Piece. From the world building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.600 --> 00:19:00.780
to the characters, to the story, this is a&nbsp;
must-read piece of media. Experiencing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:05.760
story live along with a dedicated fan&nbsp;
community isn’t something you want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:09.600
miss out on. And once you get caught up,&nbsp;
you can always come back to the channel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:16.800
to enjoy some of these theory and character&nbsp;
analysis videos. Or you can start right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:20.820
by watching the best one piece&nbsp;
theory you will ever see, i guess.

